<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Chanel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a>–<a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Peter Chanel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Chanel (1803–1841) was a French Catholic priest of the Marist order who landed on Futuna in 1837 as one of the first missionaries in the western Pacific. After a son of the island's king Niuliki sought baptism, men from the king's household killed him on 28 April 1841. Futuna turned Catholic soon afterwards; Chanel was canonised in 1954 and is the patron saint of Oceania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-chanel.jpg" alt="Pierre Chanel" width="207" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Chanel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
